# A master's trade (Docs/Design/83-dialogue-trees.md, Phase 3): from a resident's "Could you teach me your trade?" and
# the wheel's Apprentice. Every trade can be learned (the living-NPC roadmap): the work and its hours, what it pays,
# what it takes to be taken on, and asking (World::apprentice: a master takes one apprentice at a time, and one they
# know and trust, a regard of 30). Any work the master's market has goes on in the work tree.
#
# here.teaches: they hold a trade (not the watch) and have no apprentice. here.take_on and here.take_on_why: whether
# they'd take this wolf on now, and why not. here.trade_title: the trade.

tree master
entry learn learn

node learn
say #here.trade_title.capitalize#? #learn_offer# What do you want to know? | #learn_offer# Ask away.
say[here.teaches=no priority=2] I've an apprentice already, I'm afraid. But ask what you like.
free
choice What's the work like? -> work
choice What does it pay? -> wages
choice What would it take to learn it? -> takes
choice Will you take me on? [here.take_on=yes] locked "#here.take_on_why#" -> do apprentice ; then taken ; refused refused
choice Any work going? [here.giver=yes] -> do open work
choice Something else... -> do open chat
choice Goodbye. -> bye

node work
ask player.hours
say Long days, but honest ones. | Steady work, most days.
free
choice What does it pay? -> wages
choice Will you take me on? [here.take_on=yes] locked "#here.take_on_why#" -> do apprentice ; then taken ; refused refused
choice Goodbye. -> bye

node wages
say Nobody pays a wage to learn. You work beside me and learn it three times as fast as alone; what you make, you sell.
free
choice What would it take to learn it? -> takes
choice Will you take me on? [here.take_on=yes] locked "#here.take_on_why#" -> do apprentice ; then taken ; refused refused
choice Goodbye. -> bye

node takes
say I take one apprentice at a time, and one I know and trust. You'd do. Ask, and it's settled.
say[here.take_on=no priority=2] One apprentice at a time, and one I know and trust. #here.take_on_why#
free
choice Will you take me on? [here.take_on=yes] locked "#here.take_on_why#" -> do apprentice ; then taken ; refused refused
choice What's the work like? -> work
choice Goodbye. -> bye

node taken
say Good. Be here when I start, and stay near me while I work. | Then you're mine to teach. Stay close while I work.
mood pleased
choice Goodbye. -> bye

node refused
say #topic.why# | Not yet. #topic.why#
choice Goodbye. -> bye

node bye
say #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#. | Mind how you go.
end
